mode: "100644"
text: "# The STORY framework — run a launch as one story across the phases\n\nThe #1 lesson: a launch is **one story across three phases**, not three disconnected campaigns. STORY wraps\nthat arc with a goal up front and measurement at the end. The agent **plans + writes the posts + the brief**;\n**WoopSocial schedules + publishes the coordinated social posts** on the timeline; the **waitlist/hub, email,\nads, checkout, press, and livestream are external/native.**\n\n## S — Set one goal + the brief\n- **One primary goal** (the success metric). Pick the **launch type** (soft / hard / phased). **1–3\n  platforms.** Write the **one-page launch brief** (what's launching, who it's for, why now, the offer, who\n  owns what, the timeline). **Discipline over speed.**\n\n## T — Tease to build demand (pre-launch)\n- **Emotional investment** before the offer exists. **Waitlist** (specific promise; pre-launch marketing ≈\n  +30% day-one sales — vendor, directional) + **referral.** **One campaign hub** all links point to. **BTS / teasers / proof drops**; a **beta group**\n  (50–200); **personalized press/creator outreach** (10–20, not a mass release).\n\n## O — One coordinated launch (launch day)\n- **Concentrate the push** across channels in a short window (**velocity is rewarded**). **One CTA**, remove\n  friction. **Credible urgency** — real scarcity / meaningful bonus / honest deadline, **never fake/resetting\n  timers.** A **timed drop / countdown / live** for the peak.\n\n## R — Reinforce with proof (post-launch)\n- **Compound trust:** testimonials, UGC, demos, objection-answers, FAQs. **Sustain** — don't go quiet while\n  people are deciding. Close the **signed-up → used** gap (simplify onboarding).\n\n## Y — Yield: measure + debrief\n- Read **numbers vs targets per channel** (day-one conversions, signups, referral, ROI). Debrief what\n  worked/broke; **feed the next campaign.** Never fabricate results.\n\n## The launch plan a request should fill\n```\nGOAL: one primary goal + metric; launch type (soft/hard/phased); 1-3 platforms; one-page brief\nTEASE: waitlist (specific promise) + referral; one hub; BTS/teasers/proof; beta 50-200; personalized press/creator outreach\nLAUNCH: coordinated concentrated push; ONE CTA + remove friction; credible urgency (no fake timers); drop/countdown/live\nREINFORCE: proof (testimonials/UGC/demos/objections); sustain; onboarding to first value\nYIELD: numbers vs targets per channel; debrief; never fabricate. WoopSocial schedules/publishes the social posts; hub/email/ads/checkout/press/live external\n```\n"
